.Dd $Mdocdate: September 17 2026 $
.Dt CLI-CLAP-GENERATED 1
.Os
.Sh NAME
.Nm cli-clap-generated
.Nd an example generated using the cli template
.Sh SYNOPSIS
.Nm cli-clap-generated
.Op Fl hVv
.Op Ar arg ...
.Sh DESCRIPTION
.Nm
is a template command line tool.
It logs to
.Em stderr
and prints a greeting to
.Em stdout .
.Pp
The options are as follows:
.Bl -tag -width Ds
.It Fl h , Fl -help
Print usage and exit.
.It Fl V , Fl -version
Print the version, git hash and build date, then exit.
.It Fl v , Fl -verbose
Produce more verbose output.
Once enables debug messages, twice enables trace messages.
.El
.Sh ENVIRONMENT
.Bl -tag -width CLI_CLAP_GENERATED_LOG
.It Ev CLI_CLAP_GENERATED_LOG
Log filter in
.Sy env_logger
syntax, for example
.Ql debug
or
.Ql cli_clap_generated=trace .
Takes precedence over
.Fl v .
.El
.Sh EXIT STATUS
.Ex -std
.Sh EXAMPLES
Print the version:
.Pp
.Dl $ cli-clap-generated -V
.Pp
Run with trace output:
.Pp
.Dl $ cli-clap-generated -vv foo bar
.Sh AUTHORS
.An your name Aq Mt author@example.com
